<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<CustomField xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        FSD TRANCHE 2, ITEM 3 (2026-08-16) - WHY THIS FIELD EXISTS AND WHAT EACH BRANCH MEANS.
        This note lives in a comment, not in <description>, and is INSIDE the root element on
        purpose - a comment ABOVE <CustomField> breaks the sf deploy at conversion with a
        misleading "unable to find matching parent xml file". Precedent: Deal_Bucket__c.

        (i) WHY THIS FIELD EXISTS AT ALL. A Salesforce list-view filter cannot traverse a
        lookup. The FSD's five LOI/PSA sub-states (Pending/Submitted/Accepted,
        Negotiation/Executed) are CHILD-RECORD states living on LOI__c / Contract_Review__c,
        not on Opportunity. This same-object text formula is what makes them filterable, the
        exact mechanism Deal_Bucket__c already uses for its own five buckets.

        (ii) DEAD IS TESTED FIRST AND RETURNS BLANK, so all five Deal_Tracker_LOI_*/PSA_*
        list views inherit the dead exclusion for free and cannot drift from it - same shape
        as Deal_Bucket__c's own dead clause.

        (iii) A BLANK Primary_LOI__c / Primary_Contract__c FALLS TO THE ENTRY STATE, NOT TO
        BLANK. Primary_LOI__c / Primary_Contract__c are stamped only for the child
        OpportunityReviewService itself creates (ARCHITECTURE.md §2), so an irregularly
        created child leaves the lookup null. A deal sitting at the LOI stage with no LOI
        record genuinely IS "LOI - Pending" - failing to a meaningful bucket beats dropping
        the deal out of every view.

        (iv) ACQUISITION-ONLY, STRUCTURALLY. Reaching through Primary_LOI__c from an
        Opportunity can only ever reach an acquisition LOI - a disposition LOI hangs off
        Disposition__c and has no Opportunity lookup at all. That matters because
        LOI__c.Stage__c's acquisition and disposition value sets overlap at 'Under Review'
        (see that field's own header) - this formula never reads Stage__c and never reaches a
        disposition row, so the overlap cannot mislead it.

        (v) LOI_Approved__c MEANS "DPEG approved SENDING the LOI", NOT "the seller accepted"
        (see that field's own <description>) - that is exactly the Pending -> Submitted
        boundary this formula draws.

        (vi) Contract_Signed__c IS STAMPED BY ContractExecutionService AT PSA EXECUTION.
        ⚠ That field's own <description> currently reads "Checked when the LOI is fully
        executed" - THAT DESCRIPTION IS STALE AND WRONG; the class header is authoritative.
        Flagged as a finding, not corrected here (out of this item's scope).

        (vii) 🔴 UNVERIFIED - THE SINGLE HIGHEST-RISK ASSUMPTION IN THIS FIELD.
        Deal_Bucket__c proves a SAME-OBJECT formula is filterable in a Salesforce list view.
        It does NOT prove a CROSS-OBJECT one is. Three of the five branches below
        (PSA - Executed, PSA - Negotiation, LOI - Pending) read only same-object fields
        (Contract_Signed__c, LOI_Approved__c) so they are unaffected either way. The two that
        read Primary_LOI__r.LOI_Signed__c (LOI - Submitted, LOI - Accepted) are the ones at
        risk. VERIFY IN ORG BEFORE TRUSTING THE DEPLOY: save one of the five
        Deal_Tracker_LOI_*/PSA_* list views by hand and confirm it actually filters (post-
        deploy gate G2). NAMED FALLBACK if it fails: a Checkbox on Opportunity maintained by
        the already-live flows/LOI_Signed_Notify (which fires on exactly
        LOI__c.LOI_Signed__c = true), turning the formula fully same-object. Do not build
        that fallback speculatively.

        Uses ISPICKVAL(...), never == on a picklist, and never ISPICKVAL on LOI__c.Stage__c -
        the standing repo rule, because 'Prepare/Review' carries a literal slash.
    -->
    <fullName>Deal_Sub_Stage__c</fullName>
    <description>LOI/PSA sub-stage for list-view filtering, derived from stage + child-record signature. Reporting-only projection - automation must branch on StageName/LOI__c/Contract_Review__c fields directly, never on this formula (before-save flows cannot read formula fields). See the XML comment on this file for the branch-by-branch rationale.</description>
    <externalId>false</externalId>
    <formula>IF( OR( ISPICKVAL(StageName, &apos;Dead/Pass&apos;), ISPICKVAL(Deal_Category__c, &apos;Dead&apos;) ), &apos;&apos;,
IF( ISPICKVAL(StageName, &apos;LOI&apos;),
      IF( AND( NOT(ISBLANK(Primary_LOI__c)), Primary_LOI__r.LOI_Signed__c ), &apos;LOI - Accepted&apos;,
      IF( LOI_Approved__c,                                                    &apos;LOI - Submitted&apos;,
                                                                              &apos;LOI - Pending&apos; ) ),
IF( ISPICKVAL(StageName, &apos;Under Contract (PSA)&apos;),
      IF( Contract_Signed__c, &apos;PSA - Executed&apos;, &apos;PSA - Negotiation&apos; ),
      &apos;&apos; ) ) )</formula>
    <formulaTreatBlanksAs>BlankAsBlank</formulaTreatBlanksAs>
    <label>Deal Sub Stage</label>
    <required>false</required>
    <trackTrending>false</trackTrending>
    <type>Text</type>
    <unique>false</unique>
</CustomField>
